Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(config): add upstream.meta.reasoning-replay switch

Default off. Optional model patterns scope it to a canary, matched against both the
requested name (including oauth model aliases) and the upstream model.
---
 config.example.yaml                           |  19 ++++
 internal/config/config.go                     |   3 +
 internal/config/config_types.go               |  72 ++++++++++++
 internal/config/config_v8.go                  |   2 +-
 internal/config/meta_reasoning_replay_test.go | 103 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 198 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 internal/config/meta_reasoning_replay_test.go

diff --git a/config.example.yaml b/config.example.yaml
index dd93a012..6b74e712 100644
--- a/config.example.yaml
+++ b/config.example.yaml
@@ -417,6 +417,25 @@ upstream:
     # The injected tool is also added to tool_choice.allowed_tools when applicable.
     inject-x-search: false
 
+  meta:
+    # Replay a Muse model's own reasoning back to it on later tool turns, safely.
+    # Meta binds each reasoning envelope to the account that issued it and rejects a replay through
+    # any other account, and a client resends the whole history on every turn, so envelopes from
+    # several pool accounts end up mixed in one request. When enabled the proxy tags every
+    # envelope it returns (Anthropic thinking signature or Responses encrypted_content, streaming
+    # or not) with the issuing account, forwards an envelope only when the credential selected for
+    # the request is the one that issued it, and drops every other or untagged one - the behavior
+    # without this feature. If Meta still rejects a replayed envelope the request is retried once
+    # without any, so the 400 never reaches the client. Each request that carried envelopes logs
+    # "meta reasoning replay: kept=N dropped_foreign=N dropped_untagged=N" for measuring the hit rate.
+    # Turning it off again is safe: tagged envelopes from earlier turns are dropped like any other.
+    reasoning-replay:
+      enabled: false # default false: envelopes are neither tagged nor replayed
+      # Limit the feature to matching models for a canary ("*" wildcards, case-insensitive; both the
+      # requested name, including an oauth.model-alias, and the upstream model are tested).
+      # Empty or omitted means every Meta model once enabled.
+      # models: ["muse-canary*"]
+
 # API-key upstreams are separate from access.api-keys (client authentication).
 # Each provider contains named groups: one base-url, shared settings, and a keys list.
 # Add another group for another endpoint; base-url belongs to the group, not a key.
